 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Explicit Normalization:** Using explicitly normalized surface normals ($\hat{\mathbf{n}} / ||\hat{\mathbf{n}}||$) causes training instability and degenerate results (PSNR 16.72 vs 22.24). The model relies on regularization to approximate unit vectors naturally [S1].
-*   **Initial Normal Quality:** In the initial training stage, estimated normals are not unit vectors ($||\hat{\mathbf{n}}||^2$ far from 1). The masking strategy and orientation loss help concentrate $||\hat{\mathbf{n}}||^2$ close to 1 over time [S1].
+*   **Explicit Normalization:** Using explicitly normalized surface normals ($\hat{\mathbf{n}} / ||\hat{\mathbf{n}}||$) causes training instability and degenerate results (PSNR 16.72 vs 22.24) [S1]. The model relies on regularization to approximate unit vectors naturally [S1].
